nation applied to the existence fact F002, choose a witness w in W with w nonzero; its private identity is used only in this branch. Since b_0,...,b_lambda were established in S004 as a K-basis of M tensor_Z K, there are unique scalars c_0,...,c_lambda in K with w=sum_i c_i b_i. At least one coefficient is nonzero, since if all c_i were zero the displayed expansion would give w=0, contrary to the witness property. Choose an index i in the range 0<=i<=lambda with c_i nonzero; establish this existential fact before selecting i.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"w\",\"W\",\"b_i\",\"K\",\"lambda\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F003\",\"statement\":\"There exists an index i with 0<=i<=lambda and c_i is nonzero.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"integer index from 0 through lambda\"}],\"objects\":[\"lambda\",\"c_i\",\"K\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/-\",\"value\":{\"id\":\"S007\",\"text\":\"By existential elimination from F003 choose such an index i. For every j with 0<=j<=lambda, matrix-unit action gives E_j,i w=c_i b_j. Because W is invariant under x and y it is invariant under E_j,i, so E_j,i w lies in W. The scalar c_i is nonzero in the field K and hence invertible; since W is a K-subspace, b_j=c_i^{-1}E_j,i w lies in W. This holds for each basis vector b_j, so W is the whole module. The chosen w and i are used only under L1.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F003\"],\"objects\":[\"w\",\"i\",\"j\",\"E_i,j\",\"W\",\"K\",\"b_i\",\"c_i\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/-\",\"value\":{\"id\":\"S008\",\"text\":\"The zero-subspace branch and the branch under L1 both establish that W is either zero or the whole module; discharge L1 by the two-case argument. The module has dimension lambda+1, which is positive because lambda>=0, so it is nonzero. Therefore it is irreducible as stated, including lambda=0 and p=2.\",\"uses\":[\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"W\",\"lambda\",\"M\",\"K\",\"L(K)\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L1\"]}},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/19/end\",\"value\":\"S008\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"L1\",\"type\":\"assumption that W is nonzero\",\"scope\":\"nonzero-W-branch\",\"start\":\"S005\",\"end\":\"S008\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Temporarily assume that the arbitrary invariant subspace W is nonzero; this assumption is discharged by the zero/nonzero case argument.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"W\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"w\",\"type\":\"vector in M tensor_Z K\",\"scope\":\"nonzero-witness\",\"start\":\"S006\",\"end\":\"S007\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose w in W with w nonzero using the earlier local existence fact F002.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"W\",\"M\",\"K\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"c_i\",\"type\":\"K-scalar coordinates of w in the b-basis\",\"scope\":\"coordinates-of-w\",\"start\":\"S006\",\"end\":\"S007\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define the unique coordinates c_i in K by the expansion of the already selected vector w in the already established K-basis b_0,...,b_lambda.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"H002\",\"H003\"],\"from_local\":[\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"w\",\"b_i\",\"K\",\"lambda\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"integer index 0<=i<=lambda with c_i nonzero\",\"scope\":\"selected-coordinate\",\"start\":\"S007\",\"end\":\"S007\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose i with 0<=i<=lambda and c_i nonzero using the local existence fact F003.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F003\"],\"objects\":[\"