_i,j. Let W be arbitrary. If W=0, it is the zero subspace. For the other case, temporarily assume L1: W is nonzero. By the definition of nonzero subspace, there exists a vector w in W with w nonzero; record this existence before selecting w in S006.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/objects\",\"value\":[\"R\",\"Z\",\"p\",\"r\",\"lambda\",\"X_r\",\"Y_r\",\"x\",\"y\",\"E_i,j\",\"i\",\"j\",\"K\",\"W\",\"b_i\",\"module dimension\",\"factorials\",\"binomial coefficients\"]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/introduces\",\"value\":[\"L1\"]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/produces\",\"value\":[{\"id\":\"F002\",\"statement\":\"There exists w in W such that w is nonzero.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"w\",\"type\":\"vector in M tensor_Z K\"}],\"objects\":[\"W\",\"M\",\"K\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\"]}]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/discharges\",\"value\":[]},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/-\",\"value\":{\"id\":\"S006\",\"text\":\"By existential elimination applied to the existence fact F002, choose a witness w in W with w nonzero; its private identity is used only in this branch. Since b_0,...,b_lambda were established in S004 as a K-basis of M tensor_Z K, there are unique scalars c_0,...,c_lambda in K with w=sum_i c_i b_i. At least one coefficient is nonzero, since if all c_i were zero the displayed expansion would give w=0, contrary to the witness property. Choose an index i in the range 0<=i<=lambda with c_i nonzero; establish this existential fact before selecting i.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"w\",\"W\",\"b_i\",\"K\",\"lambda\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F003\",\"statement\":\"There exists an index i with 0<=i<=lambda and c_i is nonzero.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"integer index from 0 through lambda\"}],\"objects\":[\"lambda\",\"c_i\",\"K\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/-\",\"value\":{\"id\":\"S007\",\"text\":\"By existential elimination from F003 choose such an index i. For every j with 0<=j<=lambda, matrix-unit action gives E_j,i w=c_i b_j. Because W is invariant under x and y it is invariant under E_j,i, so E_j,i w lies in W. The scalar c_i is nonzero in the field K and hence invertible; since W is a K-subspace, b_j=c_i^{-1}E_j,i w lies in W. This holds for each basis vector b_j, so W is the whole module. The chosen w and i are used only under L1.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F003\"],\"objects\":[\"w\",\"i\",\"j\",\"E_i,j\",\"W\",\"K\",\"b_i\",\"c_i\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/-\",\"value\":{\"id\":\"S008\",\"text\":\"The zero-subspace branch and the branch under L1 both establish that W is either zero or the whole module; discharge L1 by the two-case argument. The module has dimension lambda+1, which is positive because lambda>=0, so it is nonzero. Therefore it is irreducible as stated, including lambda=0 and p=2.\",\"uses\":[\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"W\",\"lambda\",\"M\",\"K\",\"L(K)\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L1\"]}},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/19/end\",\"value\":\"S008\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"L1\",\"type\":\"assumption that W is nonzero\",\"scope\":\"nonzero-W-branch\",\"start\":\"S005\",\"end\":\"S008\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Temporarily assume that the arbitrary invariant subspace W is nonzero; this assumption is discharged by the zero/nonzero case argument.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"W\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"w\",\"type\":\"vector in M tensor_Z K\",\"scope\":\"nonzero-witness\",\"start\":\"S006\",\"end\":\"S007\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose w in W with w nonzero using the earlier local existence fact F002.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"W\",\"M\",\"K\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"c_i\",\"type\":\"K-scalar coordinates of w in the b-basis\",\"scope\":\"coordinates-of-w\",\"start\":\"S006\",\"end\":\"S007\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define the unique coordinates c_i in K by the expansion of the already selected vector w in the already established K-basis b_0,...,b_lambda.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"H002\",\"H003\"],\"from_local\":[\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"w\",\"b_i\",\"K\",\"lambda\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"integer index 0<=i<=lambda with c_i nonzero\",\"scope\":\"selected-coordinate\",\"start\":\"S007\",\"end\":\"S007\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose i with 0<=i<=lambda and c_i nonzero using the local existence fact F003.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F003\"],\"objects\":[\"c_i\",\"lambda\"]}}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration","module"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible; choose a narrow pointer for large objects.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"f4347ee2-3775-4a39-8f8c-c5d404588ce9","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"